WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.123
This video covers who may manage connections and data sets, and how to

00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:08.974
copy them to another site, such as from staging to the live site,

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:10.547
with a deployment plan.

00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:13.910
It ends with what to check when something does not work.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.210
Five permissions cover data connectors.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:27.870
Manage data connections and their credentials is for creating, editing, testing and deleting connections.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:32.070
It is security critical, because a connection holds credentials.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.031
Manage connected data sets is for data sets.

00:00:36.031 --> 00:00:42.710
Refresh imported data sets lets someone run Refresh now, and is included in the manage permission.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:48.250
Read every connected data set, or Read the connected data set with one

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.473
name, decide who can use a data set in reports and pipelines.

00:00:52.473 --> 00:00:55.750
Administrators have the first four by default.

00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:04.653
Open a role in Access Control, Roles, and find the Data Connectors group.

00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:09.414
Manage data connections and their credentials is marked security critical:

00:01:09.414 --> 00:01:13.222
give it only to the people who look after the connections.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:19.260
Manage connected data sets lets a person create, edit, preview and delete data sets.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.308
Allow it and save the role.

00:01:21.308 --> 00:01:26.274
When you open the role again, Refresh imported data sets is effective too,

00:01:26.274 --> 00:01:29.253
because the manage permission includes it.

00:01:29.704 --> 00:01:35.564
Refresh imported data sets can also be given alone, to someone who may only refresh.

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:41.202
And Read every connected data set includes the read permission of each data set.

00:01:41.202 --> 00:01:45.184
That is the permission the reports and pipelines video used.

00:01:49.357 --> 00:01:54.077
To copy connections and data sets to another site, use a deployment plan.

00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:58.737
Under Deployments, Plans, click Add Deployment Plan, and give it a name.

00:01:59.192 --> 00:02:03.653
Click Add Step, open the Data group, and add Data Connections.

00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:09.492
Leave Include all connections ticked, or clear it and tick the connections to copy.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.438
Then add Connected Data Sets in the same way.

00:02:14.438 --> 00:02:16.448
Keep the connections first:

00:02:16.448 --> 00:02:20.041
each data set needs its connection on the other site.

00:02:20.492 --> 00:02:25.362
Execute the plan to download its file, or to send it to another site.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:29.622
On the other site, import the file in Package Import.

00:02:29.622 --> 00:02:33.562
That site needs the Deployment and Recipes features on.

00:02:37.762 --> 00:02:42.322
A connection or data set with the same identifier or technical name is

00:02:42.322 --> 00:02:44.842
updated, and the others are created.

00:02:45.592 --> 00:02:50.855
Passwords, keys and secrets are not copied, because they are encrypted for the

00:02:50.855 --> 00:02:52.547
site that holds them.

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:57.372
Open each copied connection, type its secrets, and click Save and test.

00:02:58.122 --> 00:03:00.786
Imported data sets don't bring their rows.

00:03:00.786 --> 00:03:04.837
Each one starts its first import on the other site within a minute,

00:03:04.837 --> 00:03:06.502
from its own connection.

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:11.363
The other site needs the same connector features turned on, and it must

00:03:11.363 --> 00:03:13.232
be able to reach the systems.

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:21.807
If a data set is missing from reports, check that it is enabled.

00:03:21.807 --> 00:03:25.885
A disabled data set is not listed to reports and pipelines.

00:03:26.335 --> 00:03:30.588
Check that its fields were read, with Discover fields, and that your role

00:03:30.588 --> 00:03:32.095
is allowed to read it.

00:03:32.547 --> 00:03:36.952
An imported data set shows no rows until its first refresh succeeds.

00:03:36.952 --> 00:03:39.154
Open its History for the error:

00:03:39.154 --> 00:03:42.547
the last good rows stay available while you fix it.

00:03:42.547 --> 00:03:46.357
And if a check says the host is on the site's own network,

00:03:46.357 --> 00:03:48.797
ask your administrator to allow it.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:55.305
Give the manage permissions to the few who look after connections, copy them

00:03:55.305 --> 00:03:59.154
with a plan, type the secrets again on the other site, and check

00:03:59.154 --> 00:04:01.298
the history when a refresh fails.

00:04:01.298 --> 00:04:02.727
Thanks for watching.

